#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041b2509-a556-5b7c-ab45-9ca5fd9c3cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-15{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436753} {:answer/id #uuid "08e24a6d-b6f5-53e0-a5c7-349a5368a361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=15{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436757} {:answer/id #uuid "6c046924-1709-5274-a794-1f3b95605dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=15{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436775} {:answer/id #uuid "7e45231b-e9d5-5367-ad87-33c31af8b88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-15{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436779} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2d5e69-ef35-54de-a461-09d176c29c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436780} :answer-field/id #uuid "3095f9c5-6e39-53cb-accf-8b0a4693c3a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0469c521-df52-516d-97d5-643098592b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-130841" :question/problem "Let  $E=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-15$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-15{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2034d0-7cda-5f39-9589-90aba5659d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436758} {:answer/id #uuid "49fe98f4-4ffc-5af2-83a4-d3f36bfa74f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436770} {:answer/id #uuid "4d910c4e-a0ac-50d5-9159-50d27df48002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436771} {:answer/id #uuid "7a31368e-5bda-5127-82e3-a85cb11c6a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436778} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6c5718-69bf-54af-9c04-7a6648adfb74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436790}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436770} :answer-field/id #uuid "98133f54-d0b4-500e-be6b-d23f4be79f09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "338846a1-5093-5e28-a69f-a5c5dede7770" :question/math-academy-id "q-130863" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}=7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46c940ea-d23e-573b-94e4-9b08dcb0d527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-8){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436767} {:answer/id #uuid "4833bf41-8721-53ee-a05b-eef1d1d7ffbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-8{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436768} {:answer/id #uuid "74604d91-78d7-5d75-a2b1-c1116cb378c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436777} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6ef404-d51f-5dc8-8232-ced9b78b97ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=8{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436794} {:answer/id #uuid "eb024a6c-2255-51f9-a1ab-f1df1f59e9cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436797}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436797} :answer-field/id #uuid "a02475ca-ca51-5bbb-9fb2-8ed70c95ef71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "45f3ee1a-e687-51c7-8953-3c231936ec3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75075" :question/problem "Let $E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-8$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bdc6917-9114-570c-b655-0097a2be410a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436774} {:answer/id #uuid "86b0d865-71ce-5220-9638-642262d571c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436782} {:answer/id #uuid "afc0ce32-cc50-5733-b5e8-eadc123226ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436788} {:answer/id #uuid "e3990169-9d67-57a7-8327-43a5424638ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436796} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c7a979-ff9d-5864-b885-40fddca4b43c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436801}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436782} :answer-field/id #uuid "76248571-5036-5758-846c-eda5b7a6680e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e584c32-a3dd-5eaa-a4dc-b23f04848d16" :question/math-academy-id "q-42809" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e96febe-54c3-5e3a-a3b3-7bd0082d0748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436764} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1ac934-f42e-5421-a48c-557b71cea666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436784} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7860a0-b9d2-5afc-af0b-2703b7594661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436787} {:answer/id #uuid "f2338944-0fa0-5908-a315-427b16f9b9fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436799} {:answer/id #uuid "f88a4afc-f340-5d8a-8f8b-7f4abe4ed444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436802}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436799} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef5c36a4-d082-592