nd{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08df48ed-79af-5bf2-85ef-d1439433ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436756} {:answer/id #uuid "0f089b50-55e5-516b-9f45-db7bc3a03d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436759} {:answer/id #uuid "487debef-ed20-58c1-b2bb-36f8c9abf586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436769} {:answer/id #uuid "6e60ea78-a600-5e26-8bc9-6dc62c40ffde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436776} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d1e1c7-900d-5649-b458-08e60264afaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436785}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436785} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bba64a8-5bb2-5bab-90e3-aa7ac4488ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cc406c3a-4f36-5f35-99c4-51a064b8434e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75088" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e05fbe-65fb-57d3-abc5-dad8fbda182c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436754} {:answer/id #uuid "13ff5b43-6d2d-5974-abfa-8944682722ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436760} {:answer/id #uuid "4e3f1fc6-8f02-5a4d-8369-6a8d56c223fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436772} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d9b0b9-9afc-539b-a11d-4895134d5d0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436786} {:answer/id #uuid "b123dd5a-7531-527b-b537-ac54ff7d5dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436789}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436754} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2a33dc-019b-539c-8057-1ac05dffb007" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f990568f-351a-543d-9726-4bfca20a8616" :question/math-academy-id "q-75087" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$  \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d716cf-9dbc-5925-a952-39f8a779d625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 13 & -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440738} {:answer/id #uuid "46166285-4cc3-5c29-a51d-90795072a94d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 13 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440739} {:answer/id #uuid "4807c645-f441-5adc-9241-eb994ff662ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440741} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3113ad-7d59-5808-9038-62f58375aabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 13 & -5 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440742} {:answer/id #uuid "a76a29ba-6ba2-57b4-97e1-483f343e9c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 7 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 13 & -5 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440752}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440738} :answer-field/id #uuid "30c67f7d-b9fb-5337-ad56-2ae0b842b7c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "005f69e9-1456-54e0-a1fd-e854c7360e54" :question/math-academy-id "q-130879" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -3 & 13 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 19 & 2 & -7 & -5\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{32}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -3 & 13 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 19 & 2 & -7 & -5\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 13 & 0 & -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 13 & 0 & -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 13 & -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 13 & -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "333b186d-9fdb-5337-9547-777d95fd43a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 10 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440737} {:answer/id #uuid "7185b2cd-fbd5-52c7-a5b6-e9ad08779e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\begin{vmatrix}11 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 10 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440744} {:answer/id #uuid "9c7107f6-6d20-53e7-a059-e9e42ec6f1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440749} {:answer/id #uuid "dd499585-0d01-5837-9bcd-40b9e212df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440761} {:answer/id #uuid "fae70d9d-10fb-588c-adfb-03fcba2ffb5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 11 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440766}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440749} :answer-field/id #uuid "141d1b86-0b32-5f20-8147-385eaa555e9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e512d90-51a0-5df7-a85a-866294c50b88" :question/math-academy-id "q-131231" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & 6 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{24}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{24}=2$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & 6 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 3- & 7 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d041347-974c-5211-8af3-0d1eb0d54714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440748} {:answer/id #uuid "a328cadc-7951-533e-ad43-d926e5950f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440750} {:answer/id #uuid "d15147b2-fac5-5c6f-b4db-ec70e4487643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440758} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a376ea-df94-535c-826d-ac17d1f3a3ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440759} {:answer/id #uuid "e73e510a-6138-525f-beef-ac3b1cf34f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440763}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440763} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0d831e-6e0f-59da-ab3f-8c9921b69fc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3010fec5-ce32-5d13-98b7-fb9085f51f6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-91252" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 & 5\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 9 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3(3-45) \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440779 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "476634a7-3127-5dfb-8548-86988b800729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440740} {:answer/id #uuid "8677367f-731e-5786-810b-4a5834eb9e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440747} {:answer/id #uuid "c5998369-5efd-53c2-a6dc-3f4d2c8c17c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 9 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440755} {:answer/id #uuid "fb266362-88fb-55ee-b32a-0a37bb635c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440767} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc76282-8435-5ff8-9828-1f03763d49b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 4\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440767} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fccaa80-3817-5c7f-a05e-83fa6ed0c12d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4d57bf97-1629-5c5b-aa31-076c598fe8ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-131255" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -6 & -11 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{22}=2$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -6 & -11 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24b9de88-7ddb-5b58-b30d-923571de9446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440736} {:answer/id #uuid "78242538-3ed6-59de-be3c-33fa32cdeeb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440745} {:answer/id #uuid "c4eb8721-33ec-52bc-8a6e-8bb24d93b164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440754} {:answer/id #uuid "d00d7ab2-12e5-5af5-a41f-707d9c669240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 4\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440756} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a38a5e-bb09-5bb9-acfc-39240d600c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440757}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440754} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6055d74-81b9-54e0-8fc3-55044161a211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb